19. FINAL NON-NEGOTIABLE ACCEPTANCE RULES

A GitHub connector is complete only when it can access an authorized repository and execute all advertised repository operations.

An AWS connector is complete only when it authenticates, discovers the permitted account resources, evaluates their security state and saves real evidence.

A scanner is complete only when it runs, parses actual output, records findings and handles execution failures correctly.

An attack path is complete only when its relationships are derived from evidence and the result can be recalculated after a fix.

A remediation is complete only when the proposed change has been tested and its effect has been verified.

A notification is complete only when the provider reports successful delivery or the platform correctly records a delivery failure.

An MCP tool is complete only when it invokes the real backend operation under the correct user and organization permissions.

An integration is not Healthy merely because its settings are saved.

A user workflow is complete only when a real user can execute it from beginning to end.

No external credentials may be fabricated.

No customer data may be exposed between organizations.

No production security action may be performed without the required authorization.

No feature may be silently removed from the agreed product scope.

